{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01F7HCUgDwWh5YwAKEGxP52f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **`answers/01-047-overfitting-how-prevent-it.md`** — Q47: Overfitting — how prevent it?\n\nKey content:\n- **Framing:** Targets the train-val loss gap diagnostic; probes whether candidates can apply bias-variance theory to real mitigations across classical ML, deep learning, and LLM fine-tuning.\n- **5-lever prevention toolkit:** (1) more/augmented data, (2) L2 weight decay + dropout, (3) early stopping, (4) cross-validation, (5) model simplification — with LoRA rank constraint called out as an inherent regularizer for LLM fine-tuning.\n- **Concrete examples:** sklearn `max_depth` for decision trees, ResNet medical imaging fine-tune with dropout + augmentation, QLoRA rank=16 on 800 examples with AdamW weight decay.\n- **Double-descent caveat** for LLMs — can't assume overparameterized = overfits; always validate empirically.\n- **4 pitfalls** covering the most common weak-candidate mistakes (listing only L1/L2, ignoring fine-tuning context, dismissing overfitting risk in large models).\n\n**Next up:** Q48 — Imbalanced datasets — how handle?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":316,"cache_read_input_tokens":58842,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":316,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7848c4b-484f-4efd-b6a0-2486f386fbac","uuid":"c2c2bdab-ba06-45b3-bb17-ce72f458f2f4"}
